    "turn_idx": 66,
    "turn_text": "It's a very simple bill. It's a parental rights bill. It's a bill about teaching education at an age appropriate level. And for the press to have hijacked it with a statement that's clearly not in the bill, what this bill does is two things. It says that if you are Some content needs to be at a later date. And that's sexual orientation, gender identity, sexuality, those kind of issues for a five-year-old, a six-year-old, a seven-year-old, and they're not even in their brains. for those concepts. So the bill says wait until the fourth grade to teach those concepts and teach those at an age-appropriate level at that time. What any responsible teacher would do, you teach things at an age-appropriate level. The other thing that it says is you cannot put racially divisive or inherently racist concepts into any part of education. And you have to teach history in its raw and its honest form, but you can't put or spin it in a way that would be indoctrinating a student when it is not only inappropriate to ever indoctrinating a student, but is wrong and",
