  },
  {
    "episode_id": 51806,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51806.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 145,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and when you look at all of those things, we don't have the mechanism to kill them. There's no drugs out there that don't cross the line with cruel and unusual punishment. Governor DeWine has put it back in the legislators' lab. He has said, look, I'm not doing this. We don't have the product to do it. So the only two remedies that we have that would clearly I'm not even sure they'd clearly violate the eighth amendment would be to either hang these people or shoot them. Well, the public's not going to stand for that. But more importantly, the majority of the public doesn't want this anymore. They understand if you keep them in prison for the rest of their life, they're not going anywhere. And prison is not a country club. I would suggest people visiting one of the 28 prisons we have in Ohio. I'm on the prison inspection committee. It is an ugly place to live in. Period. How big is that room next to us?",
