  {
    "episode_id": 51806,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51806.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 154,
    "turn_text": "they are very small. With a huge toilet and two concrete bunk beds and a little sink and a little table. And that's it folks. So it's not a country club and the death row inmates now live in the identical setting that the regular general population do they're just in an isolated wing but they have the same privileges twenty years ago we locked death penalty folks up in an isolated cell that had a door with no window and they were only allowed out for one hour a day and they actually and i and i visited that twenty three years ago in mansfield. But we learned that that actually drove them crazy. So now they have the same opportunities as the general population. They're just isolated in their own wing and they're in the cell all to themselves. So if they were moved to the general population, it would be a two man cell. But 48% of Republicans Feel we need to get rid of the death penalty in Ohio 37% believe we should keep it and the restaurant decided those are stunning numbers. That means the majority of Republicans",
